{
    "background_story": "Kaiya was a rare and mysterious boa constrictor, known for her ovoviviparous nature. She produced eggs that hatched inside her body, giving birth to live young. In the depths of the Amazon rainforest, Kaiya made her home, wrapping her slender body around the trunks of ancient trees. Her unique reproductive process fascinated the local herpetologists, who would often visit her habitat to observe and learn. Kaiya's gentle nature and unusual characteristics made her a beloved subject of study, and she thrived under the careful attention of her human caretakers. As she grew and matured, Kaiya became a symbol of the rainforest's hidden wonders, reminding all who encountered her of the magic that lay just beneath the surface.",
